<interrogationes unitas="testa_cursus">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I run an app's dispatcher in a real window?
    <responsum symbolum="applicatio_initium testa_principale testa_cursum_incipere testa_cursum_ludum_struere" via="apps/pictor/pictor.c">Include
      testa.h, define applicatio_initium(a, forma) and a one-line
      principale that returns testa_principale(argc, argv) (libraries
      never own main). In applicatio_initium build your state in
      a->piscina (never in locals - their addresses outlive the call),
      then fill the forma - titulus, latitudo, altitudo, scala, d,
      figurae, optional fons/fons_ctx, pulsator and finis. The shell
      (lib/testa.c on macOS, running ludus_fenestra_currere;
      lib/testa_android.c on Android, entered at
      ANativeActivity_onCreate) owns the window, the loop, -fumus (XXX
      frames) and -imago, and calls finis once at the end. A forma
      failing testa_formam_probare stops the run with its causa named;
      finis still runs.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
